Move the OpenSearch (OSD) cluster snapshot repo from the local NFS-shared fs
path (muppet:/mnt/photodisk/osd-snapshots, mounted on puppy) to an S3-backed
repository-s3 snapshot repo. Surfaced during the bigstore-xfer strand while
retiring the /mnt/photodisk spinner.

Why it's clean: an S3 repo is inherently shared over HTTPS, so it removes the
whole NFS layer (nfs-server ansible role + /mnt/osd-snapshots mount + the
muppet-as-NFS-server single point of failure). Cost is ~1-2c/mo for the current
391M (11 daily snapshots, dedup near-flat) in S3 Standard — 11-nines durability,
on-demand restore (NOT Deep Archive). Bucket: osd-snapshots-berrylands-eu-west-1
(account 700630586062, eu-west-1). repository-s3 is bundled-but-not-installed in
the 3.7.0 image so needs a custom image + keystore creds. Full runbook is in the
bigstore-xfer STATE.md.

Cross-strand note: the two big bodies of work are ASTRO and AIFABRIC. This is an
astro-infra change but the OSD cluster (muppet/puppy/vole tiebreaker) is aifabric
territory — hence filing the idea here.
